# Verification

```bash
pipenv run python tests/verify.py                 # everything, in parallel (~36s)
pipenv run python tests/verify.py edges scatter   # only those modules
pipenv run python tests/verify.py -l              # list the modules
pipenv run python tests/verify.py -j 1            # one process, for a traceback
```

Exits non-zero on failure. Run it after touching anything under
`server/engine/`. The checks live in `tests/checks/`, one module per area, and
naming modules runs only those -- that is how you keep the loop short while
working. `docs/testing.md` has the module table. It checks
both hard invariants (tile independence, scale invariance) plus zoom fidelity,
colour pass-through, luminance response, edge bias, the smooth-area guard,
16-bit PNG validity, and each stage that ships at 0 (global grain, edge
softening/sanding, scatter, sharpening, film texture).

Stages that ship at 0 get their **own** checks that re-run tile independence
with the stage switched on — the default-parameter checks render straight past
them, so a kernel missing from `pad_for` would seam only there.

`ENGINE.render_view` / `render_crop` are no longer called by `main.py` but are
the **only** place the crop/zoom invariants are checked. Do not delete them.

## Trap when adding a check

`sanitize(None)` fills in **defaults, not zeros**. An override dict must zero
every *other* stage that could contribute to the same measurement — e.g. the
sanding check failed first time because `edge_jitter` defaults to 0.3 and was
adding its own wander. Zero unrelated amounts explicitly.

## Adding a module

Drop it in `tests/checks/`, decorate `run(cx)` with `@suite(name, title)`, list
it in `tests/checks/__init__.py` (`ORDER` is both the print order and the import
list) and give it a `COST` entry in `runner.py` so the pool starts it early
enough. Shared scenes belong on `Ctx` in `harness.py`, not copied per module --
several modules are measured against the same smooth-patch sigma and the same
"everything else off" dict, and copies that drifted apart would make them
disagree about what they had switched off.

Note: the static `check()` call-site count is lower than the printed total,
which counts loop iterations.
